    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0127" n="881" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3778</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-19T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 11th <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> prevention exportations to firms in
                    Latin America assisting enemy. Matter being discussed here with British mission.
                    Department glad to have data regarding activity of firms mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
